            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Persian for a rival, then the Persian for advertising."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: اعتصاب",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "اعتصاب (e'tesâb) — \"a strike\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "کارگرها برای حقوق بیشتر اعتصاب کردند. kârgarhâ barâye hoquq-e bishtar e'tesâb kardand. The workers went on strike for higher pay."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "E'tesâb kardan — to go on strike. Plural e'tesâbât."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "اعتصاب (e'tesâb) was borrowed from Arabic i'tiṣāb (EtymDB), a verbal noun usually explained as banding together; in modern Persian it is a strike."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
