          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "زحمت کشیدن (zahmat keshidan) — \"to work hard, to take pains\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "مادرم برای ما خیلی زحمت کشید. mâdaram barâye mâ kheyli zahmat keshid. My mother worked very hard for us."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Zahmat \"trouble, effort\" + keshidan \"to pull\" (stem kesh-). A polite thanks: zahmat keshidid, you went to a lot of trouble."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "زحمت was borrowed from Arabic zaḥma \"pressing, thronging\" (EtymDB); with the inherited Persian verb keshidan \"to pull, to bear\", it means to bear the trouble."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
